WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.870
Every nerve impulse is built the same way:

2
00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:05.610
a brief flip in the
voltage across a membrane,

3
00:00:05.660 --> 00:00:08.380
lasting about 1 to 2 milliseconds.

4
00:00:08.430 --> 00:00:13.060
It passes along an axon, each stretch
of membrane triggering the next.

5
00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:16.280
Yet some impulses race
along faster than a car,

6
00:00:16.330 --> 00:00:19.020
while others creep at walking pace.

7
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:23.150
Why do some nerve impulses travel
so much faster than others?

8
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:26.790
In this mission, you'll watch
a single action potential rise,

9
00:00:26.840 --> 00:00:28.760
fall and settle back.

10
00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:32.800
Then you'll compare speeds
measured in six different axons.

11
00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:38.150
Your mission: find out why some nerve
impulses race faster than a car while others

12
00:00:38.200 --> 00:00:40.050
creep along at walking pace.
